IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `crp-dates`

-- Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA) -- the rules a group member, or a person who starts a
-- representative proceeding ("class action") in the Supreme Court of Western Australia, meets.
--
-- Based on content from the Western Australian Legislation website: "Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act
-- 2022" (No. 30 of 2022, as retrieved 2026-09-07), with "Rules of the Supreme Court 1971" Order 18A (version 09-am0-00,
-- retrieved 2026-11-06) and "Interpretation Act 1984" ss 61, 62, State of Western Australia, licensed under CC BY 4.0
-- (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Quotations are from the deposited plain-text conversions at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_45801.txt and the source bundles of those subjects.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.
--
-- Negatives follow the rulings of 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05 (docs/ENCODING-GUIDE.md section 5): JUST FALSE where the
-- text itself says no; NOTHING where it does not answer, each tagged "NOTHING-kind" with the reason. Where the Court
-- decides (it "may", it is "satisfied", it "thinks fit"), JUST TRUE means the Court can do it, never that it will; the
-- Court's judgments are taken as inputs.

§ `Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022`

-- A MAYBE BOOLEAN conjunction: a no in either part is a no; otherwise an unanswered part leaves the whole unanswered.
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`both` a b MEANS
    IF (a EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (b EQUALS JUST FALSE)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF (a EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (b EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Part 1 -- which proceedings (ss 2, 4)`

-- Compilation table: "Pt. 1: 14 Sep 2022 (see s. 2(a)); Act other than Pt. 1: 25 Mar 2023 (see s. 2(b) and SL 2023/21
-- cl. 2)". Section 4 is in Part 1; sections 6 to 37 are not.
`the day Part 1 came into operation` MEANS `the day` 14 9 2022
`the day the rest of the Act came into operation` MEANS `the day` 25 3 2023

-- s 4(1) "This Act applies to a proceeding commenced on or after the day on which this section comes into operation,
-- whether the cause of action accrued before, on or after that day." Before 14 September 2022: a scope limit with no
-- "only". NOTHING-kind: scope limit (ruling (c)). From 14 September 2022 to 24 March 2023 the Act "applies" but s 6,
-- which lets a proceeding be commenced as a representative proceeding, was not yet in operation (finding 1).
-- NOTHING-kind: silent (fork F1).
GIVEN `the day it is commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 2, 4 -- Part 2 reaches a proceeding commenced that day` `the day it is commenced` MEANS
    IF `days from` `the day the rest of the Act came into operation` `the day it is commenced` AT LEAST 0
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Part 2 -- who can bring a representative proceeding (ss 6, 7, 10)`

-- s 6(1) "A proceeding may be commenced as a representative proceeding if -- (a) 7 or more persons have claims against
-- the same person; and (b) the claims of all those persons are in respect of, or arise out of, the same, similar or
-- related circumstances; and (c) the claims of all those persons give rise to a substantial common issue of law or
-- fact." s 6(3), (4): the kind of relief and separate contracts or acts make no difference, so they are not asked. s 7(2):
-- several respondents may be sued even if not every person has a claim against every respondent, so it is not asked.
-- s 10 "A representative proceeding cannot be commenced if the proceeding would be concerned only with claims in respect
-- of which the Court has jurisdiction solely by virtue of" cross-vesting. An unmet "if" (s 6) and a flat negative (s 10)
-- are the text's no.
GIVEN `the day it is commenced` IS A DATE, `how many claimants` IS A NUMBER, `same similar or related circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `substantial common issue` IS A BOOLEAN, `jurisdiction only by cross-vesting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 6, 10 -- the claims can be brought as a representative proceeding` `the day it is commenced` `how many claimants` `same similar or related circumstances` `substantial common issue` `jurisdiction only by cross-vesting` MEANS
    IF NOT (`ss 2, 4 -- Part 2 reaches a proceeding commenced that day` `the day it is commenced` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN `ss 2, 4 -- Part 2 reaches a proceeding commenced that day` `the day it is commenced`
    ELSE IF     `how many claimants` AT LEAST 7
            AND `same similar or related circumstances`
            AND `substantial common issue`
            AND (NOT `jurisdiction only by cross-vesting`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 7(1) "a person who has a sufficient interest to commence the proceeding on their own behalf against another person
-- has a sufficient interest to commence the proceeding ... as a representative proceeding". Without that interest the
-- section is silent. NOTHING-kind: silent.
GIVEN `sufficient interest on my own behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(1) -- I have standing to commence` `sufficient interest on my own behalf` MEANS
    IF `sufficient interest on my own behalf`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Rules of the Supreme Court 1971 O. 18A r. 2 "A person cannot commence or carry on a representative proceeding except
-- by a legal practitioner." A flat negative.
GIVEN `I act by a legal practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`O. 18A r. 2 -- I can commence or carry it on as I act` `I act by a legal practitioner` MEANS
    IF `I act by a legal practitioner`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 7(3) "A person who has commenced a representative proceeding retains a sufficient interest to continue the
-- proceeding and to appeal against a decision in the proceeding even if the person ceases to have a claim against the
-- respondent." A person who did not commence it (a substituted representative party) is outside the subsection's own
-- words. NOTHING-kind: scope limit (ruling (c); fork F2).
GIVEN `I commenced it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(3) -- I keep my standing without a claim` `I commenced it` MEANS
    IF `I commenced it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Who is a group member (ss 3, 8, 9)`

-- s 8(2) lists who must consent in writing (O. 18A r. 4: by filing a Form 10A and serving a copy on the representative
-- party). Everyone else needs no consent (s 8(1)).
DECLARE `Kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `an individual or a company or other person not listed`
    `the Commonwealth or a State or a Territory`
    `a Minister of the Commonwealth or of a State or Territory`
    `a public-purpose body corporate that is not an incorporated company or association`
    `an officer of the Commonwealth or a State or Territory acting as such`

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 8(2) -- consent in writing is needed` k IF
    NOT (k EQUALS `an individual or a company or other person not listed`)

-- s 3 "group member means a member of a group of persons on whose behalf a representative proceeding has been
-- commenced" (a "means" definition). s 8(2) "None of the following persons is a group member ... unless the person
-- gives written consent" (an "unless").
GIVEN `the group described includes me` IS A BOOLEAN, k IS A `Kind of person`, `I gave written consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 3, 8 -- I am a group member` `the group described includes me` k `I gave written consent` MEANS
    IF NOT `the group described includes me`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `s 8(2) -- consent in writing is needed` k AND (NOT `I gave written consent`)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `What I want to do` IS ONE OF
    `be a group member`
    `take a step in the proceeding or conduct part of it`

-- s 9(1) "person under disability means a person who, under the rules of the Court, is not permitted to bring a
-- proceeding except by the person's next friend." (2) "It is not necessary for a person under disability to have a next
-- friend merely in order to be a group member." (3) such a member "may only take a step in the representative
-- proceeding, or conduct part of the proceeding, by the group member's next friend unless the Court otherwise orders."
-- For a person not under disability the section says nothing. NOTHING-kind: scope limit.
GIVEN `I am under disability` IS A BOOLEAN, w IS A `What I want to do`, `the Court ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9 -- I need a next friend` `I am under disability` w `the Court ordered otherwise` MEANS
    IF NOT `I am under disability`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER w
         WHEN `be a group member` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `take a step in the proceeding or conduct part of it` THEN
             IF `the Court ordered otherwise` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Opting out (ss 12, 30(4))`

-- s 12(1) the Court fixes a date; (3) it may fix another date to extend the period; (2) "A group member may opt out of
-- the representative proceeding by written notice given under the rules of the Court before the date so fixed." O. 18A
-- r. 5: "a group member may opt out of a representative proceeding by filing a Form 10B." s 30(4) "A group member or
-- subgroup member cannot opt out of a representative proceeding that is an appeal proceeding." "before the date": the
-- fixed date itself is too late (finding 3; Interpretation Act s 61(1)(c)). The period is the text's own (ruling (a)):
-- outside it, JUST FALSE. A notice not given by filing a Form 10B is outside the grant's own wording. NOTHING-kind:
-- limit of a grant's wording (fork F3).
GIVEN `the opt-out date` IS A DATE, `the day I file notice` IS A DATE, `written notice filed in Form 10B` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `this is an appeal proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(2) -- I can opt out` `the opt-out date` `the day I file notice` `written notice filed in Form 10B` `this is an appeal proceeding` MEANS
    IF `this is an appeal proceeding`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `days from` `the day I file notice` `the opt-out date` AT MOST 0
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `written notice filed in Form 10B`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING

-- The last day on which notice is "before the date so fixed". No roll-over for a weekend: the date is the Court's (fork F4).
GIVEN `the opt-out date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 12(2) -- the last day to opt out` `the opt-out date` MEANS
    `the day n days after` `the opt-out date` (0 MINUS 1)

-- s 12(4) "Except with the leave of the Court, the hearing of a representative proceeding must not commence earlier than
-- the date before which a group member may opt out of the proceeding." A flat negative.
GIVEN `the hearing day` IS A DATE, `the opt-out date` IS A DATE, `the Court gave leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(4) -- the hearing can start then` `the hearing day` `the opt-out date` `the Court gave leave` MEANS
    IF `days from` `the opt-out date` `the hearing day` AT LEAST 0
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the Court gave leave`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Later claims (s 13)`

-- s 13(1), (2): on the representative party's application the Court may give leave to alter the description of the
-- group "so as to include a person -- (a) whose cause of action accrued after the commencement of the representative
-- proceeding but before such date as the Court fixes when giving leave; and (b) who would have been included in the group
-- (or would have been included in the group with the consent of the person) if the cause of action had accrued before
-- the commencement of the proceeding." (3) the date fixed may be before or after the day leave is given. Outside (a) or
-- (b) the grant's own wording does not reach the person. NOTHING-kind: limit of a grant's wording (fork F5).
GIVEN `the day my cause accrued` IS A DATE, `the day the class action began` IS A DATE, `the date the Court fixes` IS A DATE,
      `I would have been included` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13 -- the group can be altered to include me` `the day my cause accrued` `the day the class action began` `the date the Court fixes` `I would have been included` MEANS
    IF      `days from` `the day the class action began` `the day my cause accrued` GREATER THAN 0
        AND `days from` `the day my cause accrued` `the date the Court fixes` GREATER THAN 0
        AND `I would have been included`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `When it stops being a representative proceeding (ss 14, 15, 16, 17)`

-- s 14 "If, at any stage ..., it appears likely to the Court that there are fewer than 7 group members, the Court may
-- ... order that the proceeding no longer continue under this Act". s 15(2) "If the Court concludes, on application by
-- the respondent, that the cost to the respondent of identifying the group members and distributing to them the amounts
-- ... would be excessive", it may direct that it no longer continue (or stay the monetary relief); (3) "This section
-- applies only in a representative proceeding where the relief claimed is or includes monetary relief." s 16(1) "where
-- it is satisfied that it is in the interests of justice to do so because" one of (a)-(d). Each is an "if", "only" or
-- "where": none met, no order under these sections. The general power in s 34 is not answered here.
GIVEN `group members the Court thinks likely` IS A NUMBER, `money is claimed for group members` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Court concludes distribution would cost too much` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Court is satisfied under s 16` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 14, 15, 16 -- the Court can stop the representative proceeding` `group members the Court thinks likely` `money is claimed for group members` `the Court concludes distribution would cost too much` `the Court is satisfied under s 16` MEANS
    IF     `group members the Court thinks likely` LESS THAN 7
        OR (`money is claimed for group members` AND `the Court concludes distribution would cost too much`)
        OR `the Court is satisfied under s 16`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 17 "Where the Court makes an order under this Part that a proceeding no longer continue under this Act -- (a) the
-- proceeding may be continued as a proceeding by the representative party on their own behalf against the respondent;
-- and (b) on the application of a person who was a group member for the purposes of the proceeding, the Court may order
-- that the person be joined as an applicant in the proceeding." No such order: the "where" fails (JUST FALSE).
GIVEN `the Court ordered it no longer continue` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 -- I can go on with my own claim in it` `the Court ordered it no longer continue` MEANS
    IF `the Court ordered it no longer continue`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Costs (ss 18(3), 19(2), 31, 33)`

DECLARE `My part in the class action` IS ONE OF
    `a group member who is not a party`
    `a group member permitted to appear on an issue about my own claim`
    `a subgroup representative party who is not the representative party`
    `the representative party`

DECLARE `Kind of costs` IS ONE OF
    `costs of the proceeding generally`
    `costs of the issues common to the subgroup`
    `costs of an issue about one member's claim only`

-- s 31 "In a representative proceeding the Court must not award costs against a group member or subgroup member other
-- than an award against -- (a) a representative party; or (b) a subgroup representative party for costs associated with
-- the determination of the issue or issues common to the subgroup members; or (c) an individual group member for costs
-- associated with the determination of an issue that relates only to the claims of that member when the member has been
-- permitted to appear in the proceeding for the purpose of determining that issue." s 18(3): where another person is
-- appointed subgroup representative party, "that person, and not the representative party, is liable for costs
-- associated with the determination of the issue or issues common to the subgroup members". s 19(2): "the individual
-- group member, and not the representative party, is liable for costs associated with the determination of the issue".
-- JUST TRUE means the Court can order it.
GIVEN p IS A `My part in the class action`, c IS A `Kind of costs`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31 -- costs can be awarded against me` p c MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `a group member who is not a party` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a group member permitted to appear on an issue about my own claim` THEN
        CONSIDER c
        WHEN `costs of an issue about one member's claim only` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a subgroup representative party who is not the representative party` THEN
        -- s 31(b); the other kinds fall within "must not ... other than", read as reaching a subgroup representative party
        -- who is a subgroup member (fork F6).
        CONSIDER c
        WHEN `costs of the issues common to the subgroup` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `the representative party` THEN
        CONSIDER c
        WHEN `costs of the proceeding generally` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- "and not the representative party" (ss 18(3), 19(2)): a flat negative. For s 18(3) this assumes another
        -- person was appointed subgroup representative party (fork F6).
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 33(1) "If the Court is satisfied, on application by a person who is or has been the representative party or a
-- subgroup representative party ..., that the costs reasonably incurred by the person in relation to the proceeding are
-- likely to exceed the costs recoverable by the person from the respondent, the Court may order that an amount equal to
-- the whole or a part of the excess be paid to the person out of damages awarded in the proceeding." (2) "An order cannot
-- be made under this section unless the Court has made an award of damages". The most is the excess, and no more than
-- the damages awarded (fork F7).
GIVEN `damages were awarded` IS A BOOLEAN, `the representative applied` IS A BOOLEAN, `costs reasonably incurred` IS A NUMBER,
      `costs recoverable from the respondent` IS A NUMBER, `damages awarded` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 33 -- the most paid to the representative out of the damages` `damages were awarded` `the representative applied` `costs reasonably incurred` `costs recoverable from the respondent` `damages awarded` MEANS
    IF NOT (`damages were awarded` AND `the representative applied`)
    THEN JUST 0
    ELSE IF `costs reasonably incurred` AT MOST `costs recoverable from the respondent`
         THEN JUST 0
         ELSE IF (`costs reasonably incurred` MINUS `costs recoverable from the respondent`) AT LEAST `damages awarded`
              THEN JUST `damages awarded`
              ELSE JUST (`costs reasonably incurred` MINUS `costs recoverable from the respondent`)

§§ `The representative party (ss 21, 24)`

DECLARE `Whom I want replaced` IS ONE OF
    `the representative party`
    `a subgroup representative party`

-- s 21(1) "The Court may substitute another group member as representative party or another person as subgroup
-- representative party if it appears to the Court that -- (a) the representative party or subgroup representative party
-- is not able to adequately represent the interests of the group members or subgroup members (as appropriate); or (b) it
-- is otherwise in the interests of justice to do so." (2) "An order for the substitution of a representative party may
-- only be made on application by a group member and an order for the substitution of a subgroup representative party
-- may only be made on application by a subgroup member." An "if" and an "only": either unmet, no.
GIVEN w IS A `Whom I want replaced`, `I am a group member` IS A BOOLEAN, `I am a member of that subgroup` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Court finds them inadequate` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Court finds it otherwise in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21 -- the representative can be replaced on my application` w `I am a group member` `I am a member of that subgroup` `the Court finds them inadequate` `the Court finds it otherwise in the interests of justice` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the Court finds them inadequate` OR `the Court finds it otherwise in the interests of justice`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER w
         WHEN `the representative party` THEN
             IF `I am a group member` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
         WHEN `a subgroup representative party` THEN
             IF `I am a member of that subgroup` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 24(2) "A representative party who is seeking leave to settle, or who has settled, the party's individual claim may,
-- with leave of the Court, withdraw as representative party." (4) "Before granting a person leave to withdraw as a
-- representative party the Court must be satisfied that -- (a) notice of the application has been given to group members
-- in accordance with Part 3 and in sufficient time for them to apply to have another person substituted as the
-- representative party; and (b) any application for the substitution of another group member as a representative party
-- has been determined." Both are preconditions: either unmet, no. A representative party not settling their own claim
-- is outside s 24(2). NOTHING-kind: limit of a grant's wording.
GIVEN `they are settling or have settled their own claim` IS A BOOLEAN, `notice went to group members in time` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `every substitution application is determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24 -- the representative can be let withdraw` `they are settling or have settled their own claim` `notice went to group members in time` `every substitution application is determined` MEANS
    IF NOT `they are settling or have settled their own claim`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `notice went to group members in time` AND `every substitution application is determined`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Stay, settlement and damages (ss 22, 23, 25(4), 27(3))`

-- s 22 "Where a respondent in a representative proceeding commences a proceeding in the Court against a group member,
-- the Court may order a stay of execution in respect of any relief awarded to the group member in the representative
-- proceeding until the other proceeding is determined." A "where": not met, no.
GIVEN `the respondent is suing me in the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22 -- my award can be stayed` `the respondent is suing me in the Court` MEANS
    IF `the respondent is suing me in the Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 23(1) "A representative proceeding cannot be settled or discontinued without the approval of the Court." s 25(4)
-- "Unless the Court is satisfied that it is just to do so, an application for the Court's approval of a settlement of a
-- representative proceeding must not be determined unless notice has been given to group members."
GIVEN `the Court approves` IS A BOOLEAN, `group members were given notice` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Court is satisfied it is just without notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 23, 25(4) -- the class action can be settled` `the Court approves` `group members were given notice` `the Court is satisfied it is just without notice` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Court approves`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `group members were given notice` OR `the Court is satisfied it is just without notice`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 27(1)(f) the Court may "award damages in an aggregate amount without specifying amounts awarded in respect of
-- individual group members"; (3) "Except when approving a settlement, the Court is not to make an award of damages in an
-- aggregate amount ... unless a reasonably accurate assessment can be made of the total amount to which group members
-- will be entitled under the judgment." When approving a settlement the bar is out of the way and the power in (1)(f)
-- stands (fork F8).
GIVEN `this is approving a settlement` IS A BOOLEAN, `the total can be reasonably accurately assessed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(3) -- damages can be awarded as a lump sum` `this is approving a settlement` `the total can be reasonably accurately assessed` MEANS
    IF `this is approving a settlement` OR `the total can be reasonably accurately assessed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 3 -- notices (ss 25, 26)`

DECLARE `What the notice is about` IS ONE OF
    `the start of the class action and my right to opt out`
    `the respondent's application to dismiss for want of prosecution`
    `the representative party's application to withdraw`
    `money paid into Court in answer to a claim`
    `an application to approve a settlement`
    `another matter`

-- s 25(1) notice "must be given to group members" of (a)-(c); (2) "The Court may dispense with compliance ... where the
-- relief sought in a proceeding does not include any claim for damages"; (3) "If the Court so orders", notice of money
-- brought into Court; (4) settlement (see above); (5) "The Court may, at any stage, order that notice of any matter be
-- given"; (6) "as soon as practicable after the happening of the event to which the notice relates".
GIVEN m IS A `What the notice is about`, `damages are claimed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Court dispensed with notice` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Court ordered notice` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Court is satisfied it is just without notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25 -- I must be given notice` m `damages are claimed` `the Court dispensed with notice` `the Court ordered notice` `the Court is satisfied it is just without notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN `money paid into Court in answer to a claim` THEN
        IF `the Court ordered notice` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an application to approve a settlement` THEN
        -- s 25(4) bars deciding the application without notice; it does not in terms require notice (fork F9).
        IF `the Court ordered notice` OR (NOT `the Court is satisfied it is just without notice`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `another matter` THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind: silent (only s 25(5) reaches other matters, and only by order).
        IF `the Court ordered notice` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the Court dispensed with notice` AND (NOT `damages are claimed`) AND (NOT `the Court ordered notice`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 26(4) "The Court must not order that notice be given personally to each group member unless it is satisfied that it
-- is reasonably practicable, and not unduly expensive, to do so." An "unless".
GIVEN `the Court finds it reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Court finds it not unduly expensive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(4) -- personal notice to each of us can be ordered` `the Court finds it reasonably practicable` `the Court finds it not unduly expensive` MEANS
    IF `the Court finds it reasonably practicable` AND `the Court finds it not unduly expensive`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 26(7) "The failure of a group member to receive or respond to a notice does not affect a step taken, an order made,
-- or a judgment given, in a proceeding." A flat negative. With no failure the question does not arise. NOTHING-kind:
-- scope limit.
GIVEN `I failed to receive or respond to a notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(7) -- my missing a notice affects the proceeding` `I failed to receive or respond to a notice` MEANS
    IF `I failed to receive or respond to a notice`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Part 4 -- judgment and the fund (ss 28, 29)`

-- s 28(3)(c): the order constituting a fund must "specify the period (the distribution period), ending no earlier than
-- 6 months after the day on which the order is made, within which group members may make a claim for payment out of the
-- fund". The earliest last day the order can give, by Interpretation Act ss 61(1)(b) and 62(3) (fork F10).
GIVEN `the day of the fund order` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 28(3)(c) -- the earliest end of the distribution period` `the day of the fund order` MEANS
    `the last day of n months after` `the day of the fund order` 6

DECLARE `Fund party` IS ONE OF `the group member`
DECLARE `Fund action` IS ONE OF `make a claim for payment out of the fund`

-- s 28(3)(c): the distribution period is the period "within which group members may make a claim". Neither a duty nor a
-- prohibition, so a bare DO: a claim in the period leads to FULFILLED, the period passing without one to BREACH, whose
-- reason names s 28(4). Counted in days from the fund order; a claim on the last day is within the period.
GIVEN `days to the end of the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Fund party` `Fund action`
`s 28(3)(c) -- my claim in the distribution period` `days to the end of the period` MEANS
    PARTY `the group member`
    DO `make a claim for payment out of the fund`
    WITHIN `days to the end of the period`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the group member` BECAUSE "claim after the s 28(3)(c) distribution period: only the Court can allow it, under s 28(4)"

-- Runs the rule over when the claim was made. Takes no DEONTIC input and is not exported.
GIVEN `the day of the fund order` IS A DATE, `the end of the period` IS A DATE, `the day I claim` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 28(3)(c) -- my claim was in the period` `the day of the fund order` `the end of the period` `the day I claim` MEANS
    IF `days from` `the day of the fund order` `the day I claim` LESS THAN 0
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 28(3)(c) -- my claim in the distribution period` (`days from` `the day of the fund order` `the end of the period`)) 0 `the events`
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHERE
        `the events` MEANS
            LIST (EVENT `the group member` `make a claim for payment out of the fund` (`days from` `the day of the fund order` `the day I claim`)), (WAITUNTIL ((`days from` `the day of the fund order` `the day I claim`) PLUS (`days from` `the day of the fund order` `the end of the period`) PLUS 2))

-- s 28(4) "If the fund has not been fully distributed before the end of the distribution period, the Court may allow a
-- group member to make a claim after the end of the distribution period if it is just to do so." Two "if"s: either
-- unmet, no. The test is the state of the fund at the end of the period, not on the day of the late claim (finding 5).
GIVEN `the day of the fund order` IS A DATE, `the end of the period` IS A DATE, `the day I claim` IS A DATE,
      `fully distributed before the end of the period` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Court thinks it just` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28 -- I can claim from the fund` `the day of the fund order` `the end of the period` `the day I claim` `fully distributed before the end of the period` `the Court thinks it just` MEANS
    IF `s 28(3)(c) -- my claim was in the period` `the day of the fund order` `the end of the period` `the day I claim`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF     `days from` `the end of the period` `the day I claim` GREATER THAN 0
            AND (NOT `fully distributed before the end of the period`)
            AND `the Court thinks it just`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 29 "A judgment given in a representative proceeding -- (a) must describe or otherwise identify the group members
-- who will be affected by it; and (b) binds all such persons other than any person who has opted out of the proceeding in
-- accordance with this Act." An opt-out: "other than" read as the text's no (fork F12). A person the judgment does not
-- identify: NOTHING-kind: scope limit.
GIVEN `the judgment identifies me` IS A BOOLEAN, `I opted out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29 -- the judgment binds me` `the judgment identifies me` `I opted out` MEANS
    IF `I opted out`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the judgment identifies me`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Part 5 -- appeals (s 30(3))`

-- s 30(3) "If the representative party or subgroup representative party does not bring an appeal within the time
-- provided for instituting appeals, another member of the group or subgroup may, within a further 21 days, bring an
-- appeal as representing the group members or subgroup members". The time for instituting appeals is set by rules of
-- court not deposited, so the representative's last day is an input. "a further 21 days" is reckoned after that day
-- (Interpretation Act s 61(1)(b)); a last day on a Saturday or Sunday moves to the Monday (s 61(1)(e)); public holidays
-- are not computed (fork F11).
GIVEN `the representative's last day to appeal` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 30(3) -- my last day to appeal for the group` `the representative's last day to appeal` MEANS
    `the next day not a Saturday or Sunday from` (`the day n days after` `the representative's last day to appeal` 21)

-- "If ... does not bring an appeal within the time": an "if" (JUST FALSE when the representative did appeal in time);
-- "within a further 21 days": the text's own period (ruling (a)). "another member of the group or subgroup": a person who
-- is not one is outside the subsection's words. NOTHING-kind: scope limit.
GIVEN `the representative's last day to appeal` IS A DATE, `the representative appealed in time` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `I am a member of the group or subgroup` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day I file` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30(3) -- I can appeal for the group` `the representative's last day to appeal` `the representative appealed in time` `I am a member of the group or subgroup` `the day I file` MEANS
    IF `the representative appealed in time`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF NOT `I am a member of the group or subgroup`
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE IF     `days from` `the representative's last day to appeal` `the day I file` GREATER THAN 0
                 AND `days from` `the day I file` (`s 30(3) -- my last day to appeal for the group` `the representative's last day to appeal`) AT LEAST 0
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 6 -- limitation periods and champerty (ss 32, 36)`

DECLARE `Where my claim stands` IS ONE OF
    `the class action is still going`
    `I opted out`
    `the class action and its appeals ended without finally disposing of my claim`
    `my claim was finally disposed of`

DECLARE `Limitation answer` IS ONE OF
    `my limitation period is suspended`
    `my limitation period runs again` HAS `my new last day` IS A DATE
    `my limitation period had already run out when the class action began`
    `section 32 does not reach my claim`
    `my claim was finally disposed of in the class action`

-- s 32(1) "On the commencement of a representative proceeding, the running of any limitation period that applies to the
-- claim of a group member to which the proceeding relates is suspended." (2) "The limitation period does not begin to
-- run again unless either the member opts out of the proceeding in accordance with this Act or the proceeding, and any
-- appeals arising from the proceeding, are determined without finally disposing of the group member's claim." The days
-- left when the class action began are counted from the day after it began to the old last day, and added to the day it
-- runs again (fork F13).
GIVEN `my claim is in the class action` IS A BOOLEAN, `my old last day` IS A DATE, `the day the class action began` IS A DATE,
      s IS A `Where my claim stands`, `the day that happened` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Limitation answer`
`s 32 -- my limitation period` `my claim is in the class action` `my old last day` `the day the class action began` s `the day that happened` MEANS
    IF NOT `my claim is in the class action`
    THEN `section 32 does not reach my claim`
    ELSE IF `days from` `the day the class action began` `my old last day` LESS THAN 0
         THEN `my limitation period had already run out when the class action began`
         ELSE CONSIDER s
              WHEN `the class action is still going` THEN `my limitation period is suspended`
              WHEN `my claim was finally disposed of` THEN `my claim was finally disposed of in the class action`
              OTHERWISE `my limitation period runs again` (`the day n days after` `the day that happened` (`days from` `the day the class action began` `my old last day`))

-- s 36(1) "The torts of maintenance and champerty are abolished." (2) "This section does not affect ... (a) a cause of
-- action in tort for maintenance or champerty that accrued before the day on which this section comes into operation;
-- (b) a rule of law as to the cases in which a contract is to be treated as contrary to public policy or as otherwise
-- illegal." s 36 came into operation on 25 March 2023. A cause accruing on or after that day: abolished (a flat no). One
-- accruing before: s 36 leaves it to the common law. NOTHING-kind: points outside the sources.
GIVEN `the day the cause of action accrued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 36 -- I can be sued in tort for maintenance or champerty` `the day the cause of action accrued` MEANS
    IF `days from` `the day the rest of the Act came into operation` `the day the cause of action accrued` AT LEAST 0
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING
